From 38d3f634f1efa6791739daf43a900cbd7f7151c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lily Li <lali@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jul 2024 15:28:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] waylandsink: add ubwc modifier and zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1
 version3 support

To support UBWC, must upgrade zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1 from ver1 to ver3.
Then, dmabuf protocol could contain modifier information. UBWC and
other information, like security, could be transmitted from wayland
client to wayland server through this modifier channel.

To interact with upstream plugin, introduced "compression" field in
caps. This "compression" could be "linear" or "ubwc", based on
wayland server reported modifier capability.

Added NV12_10LE32 UBWC format support, it also named as Q12A or TP10.
HW decoder won't output NV12_10LE32 linear.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Lily Li <lali@qti.qualcomm.com>
Change-Id: Iaca2151570c57bf1c1118fee6b56c48e559005f6
(cherry picked from commit 0a8b6364b7ab4d59bed42c441c499a134ebbdd7c)
